# g55-fu-cu-ssh -> CORE-WIRE-G7

No Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock or workspace-hack change, no protocol row, nothing to remove from SERVICE_PENDING.

## s3-screen-source: the administrator check exists (replaces "no core code has that check")

`computer_screen_source::AccountAdmin` (`AccountAdmin::default()`, `is_admin() -> Option<bool>`) is the port of Node
`createAccountAdminCheck` (`whoami /groups /fo csv /nh`, the Administrators SID found in the token, read once per run, a failed read
answers None and is read again). The compose hookup's `ScreenPcAccessPort::account_is_admin` is `Box::pin(async move { Ok(admin.is_admin().await) })`
over one `Arc<AccountAdmin>`.

## s3-screen-source / s3-screen-input: one InputDesktop

`computer_screen_source::InputDesktop { input_desktop, consent, logon_ui }` and `computer_screen_input::InputDesktop { name, consent,
logon_ui }` are the same three facts. When the adapter between `ScreenInput` and the source's `ScreenInputHost` is written, give the
source's trait the input module's type (`name` for `input_desktop`) and delete the source's own struct and its `local_desktop` mapping
copy: the session's `ScreenHost` adapter needs only one of them.
The source's own pointer mapping stays the one mapping (`ScreenInput` no longer has a second one).

## mod line

None: `AccountAdmin` is inside `computer_screen_source.rs`; `computer_screen/installer_port.rs` made `ChildProcesses` `pub(super)` for it.
